# Lifeblood speech: topics, built from beats. The format and every fact and word are described in basics.speech.
#
# A remark on a topic is up to three beats: a reaction, then a detail or reason, then a turn to the listener. The
# last two are optional ([weather_detail?]): chatty speakers usually say them, quiet ones rarely, so the same lines
# give "Rain again." from one NPC and "Rain again. Good for the crops, I suppose. You staying dry?" from another.
# Write every beat so it reads on its own and after any other beat of its topic.
#
# Chats between NPCs stay on one topic (see ChatTopics): the opener speaks from chat_open_<topic>, and the other
# answers from chat_reply_<topic>, with its own facts (its own tastes, its own home).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The weather

== weather_react ==
Nice day.                    {weather=clear, time=day}
Lovely day for it.           {weather=clear, time=day, weather_like=love, w=2}
Not a cloud in the sky.      {weather=clear, time=day}
Too bright out.              {weather=clear, weather_like=hate, w=2}
Clear night.                 {weather=clear, time=night}
Look at those stars.         {weather=clear, time=night, sentimental, w=2}
Fine morning.                {weather=clear, time=morning}
Rain again.                  {weather=rain}
Still raining.               {weather=rain}
Ah, rain.                    {weather=rain, weather_like=love, w=2}
More rain. Wonderful.        {weather=rain, weather_like=hate, w=2}
Wet one today.               {weather=rain}
Some storm.                  {weather=storm}
Hear that thunder?           {weather=storm}
What a storm!                {weather=storm, weather_like=love, w=2}
I don't like the sound of that thunder. {weather=storm, timid, w=2}
Snowing again.               {weather=snow}
Look at that snow!           {weather=snow, weather_like=love, w=2}
Snow. Again.                 {weather=snow, weather_like=hate, w=2}
Thick fog today.             {weather=fog}
Can't see a thing in this fog. {weather=fog}
Red rain.                    {weather=blood_rain}
The sky's bleeding again.    {weather=blood_rain, w=2}

== weather_detail ==
Good for the crops, I suppose. {weather=rain}
Everything smells clean after. {weather=rain, weather_like=love, w=2}
Everything smells clean after. {weather=rain, weather_like=like}
My boots haven't been dry in days. {weather=rain, weather_like=dislike}
My boots haven't been dry in days. {weather=rain, weather_like=hate}
I'm soaked to the bone.      {weather=rain, wet=yes, w=2}
Nice to be under a roof for once. {weather=rain, outside=no}
The Cube God waters the world. {weather=rain, pious, w=2}
Makes you feel alive, a storm like this. {weather=storm, weather_like=love, w=2}
I'll be glad when it's passed. {weather=storm, weather_like=dislike}
I'll be glad when it's passed. {weather=storm, weather_like=hate}
Lightning struck a tree near here once. Split it right down the middle. {weather=storm, w=0.5}
The Cube God's in a mood.    {weather=storm, pious, w=2}
Everything goes quiet when it snows. {weather=snow, weather_like=love}
Everything goes quiet when it snows. {weather=snow, introvert}
My fingers are numb already. {weather=snow, weather_like=dislike}
My fingers are numb already. {weather=snow, weather_like=hate}
We don't get snow like this where I'm from. {weather=snow, home_climate=hot, w=2}
Anything could be out there in this. {weather=fog, paranoid, w=2}
Nobody bothers you in the fog. {weather=fog, weather_like=love}
I keep walking into things.  {weather=fog, lighthearted}
That can't be a good sign.   {weather=blood_rain}
Somebody's done something to deserve this. {weather=blood_rain, pious, w=2}
Days like this, I want to be outside. {weather=clear, weather_like=love}
Days like this, I want to be outside. {weather=clear, weather_like=like}
Too hot to do anything.      {weather=clear, climate=hot}
Cold, though.                {weather=clear, climate=cold}
Won't last, mind.            {weather=clear, pessimist, w=2}
Can't stay nice forever.     {weather=clear, pessimist}
Good day for getting things done. {weather=clear, time=day, hardworking, w=2}
Good day for a nap in the sun. {weather=clear, time=day, lazy, w=2}
I could watch the sky all night. {weather=clear, time=night, sentimental}
Not my kind of weather.      {weather_like=dislike}
Not my kind of weather.      {weather_like=hate}
Just my kind of weather.     {weather_like=love}
I don't mind it.             {weather_like=meh}

== weather_ask ==
You staying dry?             {weather=rain}
You like the rain?           {weather=rain, curious}
Keep your head down out there. {weather=storm}
Stay warm, all right?        {weather=snow, polite}
Stay warm, all right?        {weather=snow, sentimental}
Stay close in this fog.      {weather=fog, brave}
What do you make of it?
Think it'll last?
You feel it too?             {extrovert}
How are you holding up?      {polite}
Lovely, isn't it?            {weather_like=love}

# Answering someone who brought up the weather, with your own feelings about it.
== weather_reply ==
Tell me about it.            {weather_like=hate}
Tell me about it.            {weather_like=dislike}
I don't mind it, honestly.   {weather_like=meh}
I like it, myself.           {weather_like=like}
I love it.                   {weather_like=love}
It is what it is.            {serious}
Mm.                          {taciturn, w=2}
Could be worse.              {optimist}
Could be better.             {pessimist}
Weather's weather.

== chat_open_weather ==
[listener]. [weather_react] [weather_detail?] [weather_ask?]
[weather_react] [weather_detail?] [weather_ask?]

== chat_reply_weather ==
[weather_reply] [weather_detail?]

